<article class="env-lemma" id="0EH1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EH1">Lemma <span data-tag="0EH1">51.20.3</span>.</a> Let $I$ be an ideal of a Noetherian ring $A$. For all $n \geq 1$ there exists an $m > n$ such that the map $A/I^ m \to A/I^ n$ satisfies the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0G9V" data-tag="0G9V">51.20.2</a> with $e = \text{cd}(A, I)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\xi \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^{e + 1}_ A(A/I^ n, N)$ be the element constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0G9V" data-tag="0G9V">51.20.2</a> part (5). Since $e = \text{cd}(A, I)$ we have $0 = H^{e + 1}_ Z(N) = H^{e + 1}_ I(N) = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^{e + 1}(A/I^ m, N)$ by Dualizing Complexes, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0955" data-tag="0955">47.10.1</a> and <a href="/tag/0954" data-tag="0954">47.8.2</a>. Thus we may pick $m \geq n$ such that $\xi $ maps to zero in $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^{e + 1}_ A(A/I^ m, N)$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>